        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Four month names with a history of their own",
          "items": [
            "*Bealtaine* (May) is the name of a mid-spring fire festival older than Christianity in Ireland.",
            "*Lúnasa* (August) comes from *Lugh*, a god in Irish folklore, and his harvest festival *Lughnasadh*.",
            "*Samhain* (November) was the start of the year in the old calendar — and the origin of **Halloween**, still called *Oíche Shamhna* in Ireland today.",
            "*Meán Fómhair* and *Deireadh Fómhair* literally mean \"middle of autumn\" and \"end of autumn\", so the two month names also tell you when autumn happens."
          ]
        }
